Package: connectivity
Title: Multi-Resolution Landscape Connectivity
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Roozbeh", family = "Valavi", email = "roozbeh.valavi@csiro.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Implements an efficient multi-resolution least-cost algorithm for
    calculating connectivity-based biodiversity indicators, including Connected
    Habitat (connectivity-adjusted condition), the Protected Area Connectedness
    Index (PARC-connectedness), and the Bioclimatic Ecosystem Resilience Index
    (BERI). The algorithm maintains fine spatial resolution near each focal
    cell and progressively coarsens with distance, enabling large-scale
    connectivity calculations. The package accepts raster files and 'terra'
    SpatRaster objects, supports polygon analysis boundaries and tiled
    processing of large datasets, and calls the 'connectivity-core' numerical
    engine, written in 'Rust', through 'extendr'. The methodology is described
    in Valavi et al. (2026) <doi:10.32942/X2S68V>. Bundled example rasters for
    Tasmania are separately licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
